# fleet/maxutil.pin: the prebuilt max-util archive run.sh's max-util step unpacks (fleet/maxutil_pack.sh).
# Packed 2026-11-13 on the build host from a tt-metal branch (27164bf0: unit_tests_didt_max_util logs one CRC-32 per worker
# core of its last output tile, plus tt_metal/sfpi-version set to SFPI 7.85.0 build 1010, the ttnn wheel's SFPI, so the
# offline bundle's cut shares ttnn's SFPI copy) with build_Release/tt_metal/soc_descriptors; replaces b02e370b6e11 (same code
# on SFPI 7.83.0).
# Repacked 2026-11-14 (maxutil_pack.sh repack of 9fbce84eb637, same tt-metal tree) with syslib/: the 16 system libs the
# binary, libtt_metal.so and openmpi load beyond glibc and libstdc++ (libevent_core and libevent_pthreads among them), so a
# host without libevent-pthreads-2.1-7 runs it (a lab host without it ended every max-util run INCOMPLETE).
# Copies: $HOME/tray-test-dist/ on the build host and on the cluster node (one archive file each).
